---
/**
 * t60 · Soft Carrier
 *
 * The same carrier with the corners opened to 9 and the tail raked blunt
 * rather than pointed — as friendly as this silhouette gets before it stops
 * reading as a message at all.
 *
 * The tail is the lower-left corner rather than an addition to it: the left
 * edge runs straight past the bottom edge and rakes back up to it over 3
 * rows, taper 8-5-3. Because that corner is never rounded the bottom edge
 * stays 23 pixels unbroken, and that edge is what still reads as a message
 * at 16px, where the tail itself is barely a pixel and a half.
 *
 * Light from almost straight above, the shallowest band offset in the set
 * and a single key tone: the roundest of the four wants the quietest
 * direction, or the corner radius and the light source end up arguing about
 * where the top of the shape is.
 *
 * 7 tones peel inward as contour rings, one step per ring, so every band
 * bends around the corners and around the tail — Hozz's meniscus rather than
 * a rectangle dropped inside an outline. The direction is Mozz's, but spent
 * on where the bands sit instead of on extra tones: a pixel's effective
 * depth is pushed inward by up to 0.9 rings on the side facing away from the
 * light, so the meniscus is wide on the lit shoulder and the deep field
 * rises nearly to the keyline on the far one. The keyline carries it too — a
 * single key tone and the shallowest offset in the set.
 *
 * Spending the direction that way is what keeps the middle calm. The field
 * is one flat tone, 133 pixels of it, and no two touching pixels anywhere in
 * the mark are more than one tone apart.
 *
 * The face is supplied and untouched — facePathsAt at md with the compact
 * smile and the family gap of 2, which is exactly 8×8 — centred on the body
 * with the tail ignored: 7 rows of air above and 7 below, measured. Nothing
 * is cleared for it; white on the field is 6.9:1.
 *
 * 9 tones.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Soft Carrier">
